{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"history\",\"value_json\":\"[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Early forms are reported with 女 and 子 in variable positions; side-switched forms are treated as variants rather than chronological ancestors. Some Warring States bamboo forms are reported with 丑 in place of 女. These accounts do not provide a complete sequence of graphic change.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref044\\\",\\\"ref048\\\"]},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The selected oracle- and bronze-script illustrations are modern vector redrawings, not artifact photographs; their appearance does not establish a sequence of change.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref035\\\",\\\"ref036\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref024\\\"]},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In the Shang name 婦好, a separate proposal treats 好 as a possible homograph: 子 may supply the sound and represent a lineage name. This name analysis does not establish a phonetic role for 子 in ordinary 好.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref044\\\",\\\"ref048\\\"]},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A bronze inscription is reported to use 好 as a phonetic loan for 孝: the written sign was reused for another word because of a proposed sound resemblance, rather than because 好 acquired the meaning ‘filial piety’. The sound comparison is not supplied.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref044\\\",\\\"ref048\\\"]}]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/gloss\",\"value_json\":\"good; beautiful\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/status\",\"value_json\":\"historical\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"A bronze inscription is reported with 好 meaning ‘good/beautiful’. The vessel is not absolutely dated in the account, so this example does not establish the earliest attested ordinary use.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref022\\\",\\\"ref048\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/3/status\",\"value_json\":\"current\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/3/text\",\"value_json\":\"In modern Chinese, 好 means ‘good’. The consulted dictionaries also list current adverbial uses meaning ‘very’ or ‘very much’; they do not establish a general standalone sense ‘well’. The evidence does not show the dated steps from the selected inscriptional uses to current usage.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/3/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref042\\\",\\\"ref043\\\",\\\"ref049\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/0\",\"value_json\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"hao_nu_semantic\\\",\\\"subject\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"component\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"女\\\"},\\\"object\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"character\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"好\\\"},\\\"predicate\\\":\\\"semantic_component_of\\\",\\\"context_character\\\":\\\"好\\\",\\\"certainty\\\":\\\"probable\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"女 contributes ‘woman’ in the conventional associative analysis of ordinary 好.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref044\\\",\\\"ref048\\\"]}\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/1\",\"value_json\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"hao_zi_semantic\\\",\\\"subject\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"component\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"子\\\"},\\\"object\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"character\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"好\\\"},\\\"predicate\\\":\\\"semantic_component_of\\\",\\\"context_character\\\":\\\"好\\\",\\\"certainty\\\":\\\"probable\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"子 contributes ‘child’ in the conventional associative analysis of ordinary 好.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref044\\\",\\\"ref048\\\"]}\"}]}"}}
